Z||000000||8Ball||09-01-2001||07:52 PM||||I have been tryiong for going on 4 or 5 days now to get these bolts off my water pump on my 86 2.8 and I am down to 3 and they are impossible!!!! You think some dynamite might help?? I have one nut that I have soaked and soaked in wd40 to try to break it free and when I try to loosen it the bolt just flexes like it is going to break. The other 2 I just can't reach  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Man am I ever frustrated!!!<P>Randy||||reg||8
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-01-2001||08:54 PM||||Have you tried to tighten them first?<BR>Sometimes that helps to break them loose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||09-01-2001||10:17 PM||||heat em up! if you can try a heat gun, I know<BR>that sounds weird but those puppies put out some heat. I wouldnt try a flame(gas,oil, fire, just dont mix) put the heatgun to it<BR>for about 5 or 10 min just keep a close eye<BR>on it, than throw the wrench to her! ||||reg||12
Z||000003||8Ball||09-01-2001||11:18 PM||||I have tried tightening them,<BR>But I will definatly try to heat them up thanks!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||09-02-2001||09:29 AM||||Have you used any extensions on your wrench handle to give you more leverage?  Get a long pipe that'll fit over your socket wrench lever.  Heat them up and then push with even pressure on the end of the long pipe.  It should break them loose.  Just be careful not to bust the heads off the bolts!  Then you'll really be upset!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spektyr||09-02-2001||05:17 PM||||Word of caution here: be careful with the little bolts.  Don't remember what size they are, but the smallest ones that hold the pump on won't stand up to much abuse.<P>I recently replaced the waterpump on my 2.8 (luckily didn't have any trouble getting the bolts out) and I stripped one of those bolts putting the new one on.  Actually I didn't strip the bolt, I stripped the block and I wasn't even really trying to get it on tight.<P>The larger bolts seemed to take torque like you'd expect, but I'd advise being real careful with the other ones.  Get 'em on tight, but don't put any 'oomph' into it.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
